<title>USA: Timken invests $20 mln to expand N.C. plant.</title>
<headline>Timken invests $20 mln to expand N.C. plant.</headline>
<dateline>CANTON, Ohio 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Timken Co, which makes bearings and alloy steels, said Thursday it is investing $20 million to expand its Asheboro plant in Randolph County, N.C.</p>
<p>The plant will increase its use of technologies designed specifically to make its products quicker, and with more flexibility. The expansion will also increase the size range of its products.</p>
<p>The company said the investment &quot;represents a commitment&quot; to serve such industries as mining and construction.</p>
</text>
